## Summary: 25 Gaps, Prioritized

```
TIER 1 (7 items) — Platform instruction files
  Every major AI platform has a convention file it reads from repo root.
  You have 2 of 9 (copilot-instructions.md + GEMINI.md).
  Missing: CLAUDE.md, .cursorrules, .windsurfrules, .aider*, DEVIN.md,
           .continue/, cline_docs/

TIER 2 (5 items) — Dev environment
  No .devcontainer, no .vscode, no .editorconfig, no mypy config.
  Any agent spinning up a fresh environment has to guess.

TIER 3 (5 items) — Agent tooling
  No unified onboard script, no token estimator, no "what changed?" tool,
  no health check, no arxiv template tool.

TIER 4 (3 items) — Documentation
  No glossary, no capabilities matrix, no cross-repo instructions.

TIER 5 (5 items) — IDE integration
  No launch configs, no task definitions, no type checker config,
  no MCP server, no AI registry.
```

The highest-impact Copilot task would be **Tier 1 + Tier 2** — creating all 12 platform instruction files and dev environment configs in a single PR. Every file can reuse content from the existing `.github/copilot-instructions.md` and `COPILOT_ONBOARDING.md` adapted to each platform's format. Tier 3 tools require more design work but `tools/onboard_agent.py` alone would eliminate the "read 8 files in order" friction for every new agent session.